---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Icon from '../components/Icon.astro';
import { site, socials } from '../site';
import { url } from '../lib';
---
<Base title="About" description={`About ${site.name}: AI product manager and builder.`}>
  <h1>About</h1>
  <p class="lede">
    I've moved between most layers of a product: writing the code, making the strategy case,
    running the product, and starting the company.
  </p>
  <p>
    I started as an engineer at Bosch, went to BCG after an MBA, and then spent over four years at
    Prudential, first setting up a new insurer in India and later leading product on its wellness app.
  </p>
  <p>
    In 2025 I co-founded Gaido AI to fix something I'd seen up close: people in India lose
    health-insurance claims they should win, because the process is built to wear them down.
    We built AI agents that read the policy and the paperwork, write the appeal, and follow up
    until the money comes back. A regulatory change pulled our funding, and we wound down in
    September 2026. <a href={url('writing/evals-what-we-learned-at-gaido')}>I wrote about what it taught me.</a>
  </p>
  <p>
    What I care about: picking the problem with the sharpest pain, putting something real in front
    of users fast, and treating evals as the spec for anything an AI does. I still build most days.
  </p>

  <div class="section-label"><span>Get in touch</span></div>
  <p>
    I'm looking for AI product roles where I can own a product end to end. The best way to reach me
    is <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>.
  </p>
  <div class="actions">
    <a class="btn primary" href={`mailto:${site.email}`}><Icon name="email" /> Email me</a>
    {socials.filter((s) => s.icon !== 'email').map((s) => (
      <a class="btn" href={s.url} rel="me noopener" target="_blank"><Icon name={s.icon} /> {s.label}</a>
    ))}
  </div>
</Base>
